program	coercion/adopt_enum_raw_value_non_constant_refused.saw
triple	arm64-apple-darwin
twin	same
expect	error
build	refused	raw value for case `A` of enum `E` is not a compile-time constant
meets_expect	yes
log	"error: raw value for case `A` of enum `E` is not a compile-time constant"
log	"  --> examples/coercion/adopt_enum_raw_value_non_constant_refused.saw:21:12"
log	"     |"
log	" 21 |     case A = N,"
log	"     |            ^"
log	"   hint: a case's raw value is an integer CONSTANT EXPRESSION: literals (`0x100`, `0b1010`) and arithmetic, bitwise and shift operators over them, so a flag is spelled `1 << 8`. It may not name a `static` or another enum's case — an enum's cases are fixed by its own declaration, before any of those are known"
log	""
log	"1 error(s) generated"
